  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Early 16th-Century Tikkayat al-Gulshani Complex in Historic Cairo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tikkayat al-Gulshani was the first takiya, or residential religious complex, built in Cairo after the Ottoman conquest of 1517. This project, which includes documentation and planning activities for its eventual reuse by artisans, directly supports the U.S. embassys efforts to spur economic development in an area that has yet to rebound economically from the political disruptions of 2011.</narrative>
  </description>
